{"text": "Dolphins brains have evolved specialized areas dedicated to echolocation, allowing them to process acoustic information more quickly and with less energy. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> One key adaptation is the structure of the dolphins auditory pathway. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The signals from the ears are rapidly transmitted to the auditory cortex, the brain region responsible for processing sound. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However, unlike many other mammals, dolphins have a highly specialized auditory cortex with distinct areas dedicated to processing different aspects of echolocation signals. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Some areas may be responsible for analyzing the timing of echoes, while others focus on the frequency content or the intensity of the sound. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This specialization allows the dolphins brain to process echo information in parallel, rather than sequentially. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Imagine a factory assembly line, where different workers are responsible for different tasks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> By dividing the work among specialized areas, the brain can process information much faster and more efficiently. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This parallel processing reduces the cognitive load associated with echolocation, allowing dolphins to react quickly to changes in their environment.", "alignment": {"characters": ["D", "o", "l", "p", "h", "i", "n", "s", " ", "b", "r", "a", "i", "n", "s", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "e", "v", "o", "l", "v", "e", "d", " ", "s", "p", "e", "c", "i", "a", "l", "i", "z", "e", "d", " ", "a", "r", "e", "a", "s", " ", "d", "e", "d", "i", "c", "a", "t", "e", "d", " ", "t", "o", " ", "e", "c", "h", "o", "l", "o", "c", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", ",", " ", "a", "l", "l", "o", "w", "i", "n", "g", " ", "t", "h", "e", "m", " ", "t", "o", " ", "p", "r", "o", "c", "e", "s", "s", " ", "a", "c", "o", "u", "s", "t", "i", "c", " ", "i", "n", "f", "o", "r", "m", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "q", "